Emoji images: crates/tg-emoji/assets/emoji_1.webp .. emoji_8.webp

Where they come from
  Copied byte for byte from the Telegram Desktop repository
  (https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop, Telegram/Resources/emoji/emoji_1.webp ..
  emoji_8.webp, commit c2d0ad9, version 7.4.5). Telegram Desktop's build draws these sheets from
  Apple's "Apple Color Emoji" font (Telegram/codegen/codegen/emoji/generator.cpp, emoji set 0,
  "Mac"). Telegram Desktop ships them as its default emoji, and so do its forks.

License
  The emoji artwork is Apple's. It is NOT covered by Rustgram's GPL-3.0 license, and the
  Rustgram authors do not license it to you. Telegram Desktop's repository states no license for
  these images either: its LEGAL and LICENSE files cover its code.

Switching back
  To switch back to the Apache-2.0 Google Noto Emoji set (googlefonts/noto-emoji v2.042),
  revert commit 5d8fb9c1 ("tg-emoji: ship Telegram Desktop's emoji set (TGB-3010)")
  and the commit that added this notice.

